IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `salsl-dates`
IMPORT `salsl-core`

-- Long Service Leave Act 1987 (SA) -- THE SEAT OF THE WORKER: the person employed under a contract of service who has
-- earned, or is earning, long service leave; for the questions a death raises, the worker's personal representative.
-- Every question is asked as that person would ask it, from facts that person can state; SAET's and an inspector's
-- judgments are asked as conditions. The rules are in salsl-core.l4; this module restates none of them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (the Act's current
-- version, 1.7.2017, and the Long Service Leave Regulations 2017, version 1.9.2017, as the register's unauthorised
-- RTFs). State of South Australia, CC BY 4.0. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice.
-- See NOTES.md.

§ `The questions of the worker`

§§ `Does the Act cover me`

@export Does the South Australian Long Service Leave Act 1987 cover me (ss 3, 9, 16)?
GIVEN `I am employed under a contract of service` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an employee, employed under a contract of service (not an independent contractor engaged under a contract for services)
      `my other long service leave entitlement` IS AN `Other long service leave entitlement` @desc Whether you have a long service leave entitlement under something else: none; under another Act (for example a portable long service leave scheme Act or a public sector Act); under a fair work instrument under the Fair Work Act 2009 of the Commonwealth (a modern award or enterprise agreement that provides long service leave); or under an instrument given continuing effect under the Fair Work transitional Act 2009 of the Commonwealth
      `a SAET determination covers my class of workers` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the South Australian Employment Tribunal (SAET) has determined, under s 9, that the long service leave of your class of workers is worked out under a particular award, agreement or scheme instead of this Act
GIVETH A `Coverage answer`
`Does the Act cover me` MEANS
    `the coverage answer for` `I am employed under a contract of service` `other` `my other long service leave entitlement` `determination` `a SAET determination covers my class of workers`

@export Does my service in or outside South Australia earn long service leave under the South Australian Act, and can I choose another law's entitlement instead (s 4)?
GIVEN `where I served` IS A `Place of service` @desc Where the service was: in South Australia; outside South Australia while you were predominantly employed in South Australia; outside South Australia under a contract of employment whose proper law is South Australian law; or outside South Australia otherwise
      `I also have an entitlement under another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you also have a long service leave entitlement for this service under a law of the Commonwealth, another State or Territory, or another country
GIVETH AN `Accrual answer`
`Does my service accrue under the Act` MEANS
    `the s 4 answer for` `where I served` `corresponding law` `I also have an entitlement under another law`

§§ `My service`

@export Did this break or absence keep my service continuous, and does the time away count towards my years of service (s 6(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the kind of break` IS A `Kind of break` @desc What happened: a break your employer brought about, after which you were re-employed under an order of a court or SAET; a break your employer brought about to avoid its long service leave obligations; an absence allowed by your contract of service; an absence through illness or injury (including sick leave, paid or unpaid); long service leave or annual leave; another kind of leave (for example unpaid parental leave); a stand-down for slackness in trade, after which you were re-employed; a break from an industrial dispute, after which you returned under the settlement or were re-employed when it was settled; another break your employer brought about, after which you returned or were re-employed by it; or a break you brought about yourself (such as resigning), after which you were re-employed
      `SAET ordered that the break counts against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for re-employment under a court or SAET order: whether SAET ordered that the break does affect your continuity of service
      `the first day of the break` IS A DATE @desc The first day of the break (the first day you were not employed); used only for another break your employer brought about
      `the day I came back` IS A DATE @desc The day you returned to work or were re-employed; used only for another break your employer brought about
GIVETH A `Continuity answer`
`Did this break keep my service continuous` MEANS
    `the s 6 answer for` `the kind of break` `SAET ordered otherwise` `SAET ordered that the break counts against me` `from` `the first day of the break` `returned` `the day I came back`

@export Does this other period count as service with my employer: an apprenticeship, reserve service, or service with an employer that took over the business or a related company (ss 3(1), 3(3), 6(3), 6(4))?
GIVEN `the other period` IS AN `Other period` @desc The period: an apprenticeship with this employer; service in the Armed Forces of the Commonwealth other than the Permanent Forces (for example the reserves); service in the Permanent Forces; service with an employer that took over or acquired the business (or part of it), or whose business your employer took over; service with a related corporation (related under the Corporations Act 2001, or with substantially the same directors or management); service with a chain of such employers; or service with an unrelated employer
      `the day I completed the apprenticeship` IS A DATE @desc Only for an apprenticeship: the day you completed it
      `the day I entered into my contract of service` IS A DATE @desc Only for an apprenticeship: the day you entered into your contract of service with the employer after it
GIVETH A `Counting answer`
`Does this other period count as my service` MEANS
    `the counting answer for` `the other period` `apprenticeship completed` `the day I completed the apprenticeship` `contract entered` `the day I entered into my contract of service`

@export How many completed years of service do I have for long service leave (s 5(7), with s 6(2)-(4))?
GIVEN `the first day of my service` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your service with the employer (or with the first of related employers)
      `the last day to count` IS A DATE @desc The last day of service to count: today, the day before your leave starts, or the last day of your service if it has ended
      `the days that do not count` IS A NUMBER @desc Days in breaks or absences that keep your service continuous but do not count (s 6(2): other leave such as unpaid leave, stand-downs, industrial disputes, other breaks of up to two months), 0 if none
      `the days added` IS A NUMBER @desc Days of an apprenticeship (s 6(3)) or reserve service (s 6(4)) that count but fall outside the dates above, 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How many completed years of service do I have` MEANS
    `the completed years of service from` `the first day of my service` `to` `the last day to count` `less` `the days that do not count` `plus` `the days added`

§§ `My entitlement`

@export Am I entitled to long service leave yet, and how many weeks have I accrued and have left (s 5(1), (6), (7))?
GIVEN `my completed years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc Your completed years of service (a part year does not count)
      `the weeks I have taken or been paid out` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave you have already taken, or been paid in lieu of, 0 if none
GIVETH AN `Entitlement answer`
`Am I entitled to long service leave` MEANS
    `the s 5(1) answer for` `my completed years of service` `used` `the weeks I have taken or been paid out`

@export Can I cash out my long service leave by agreement with my employer (s 5(1a), with ss 8(3a), 10(2a), 10(7))?
GIVEN `my completed years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc Your completed years of service
      `it is an individual agreement with my employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was individually negotiated between you and your employer (not an enterprise agreement)
      `it is in writing and signed by us both` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement is recorded in writing and signed by both you and your employer
      `it was made after the leave accrued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the agreement was made after the leave being cashed out had accrued to you
GIVETH A `Cashing out answer`
`Can I cash out my long service leave` MEANS
    `the s 5(1a) answer for` `my completed years of service` `individual` `it is an individual agreement with my employer` `written` `it is in writing and signed by us both` `after accrual` `it was made after the leave accrued`

§§ `My pay`

@export What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay for long service leave, or for a payment instead of it (ss 3(2), 3(4), 8(3a)(a), 8(4)(a))?
GIVEN `how I am paid` IS A `Basis of pay` @desc How you are paid: a weekly rate; commission or another system of payment by result; or hourly, with varied ordinary hours, or casual or part-time at some time in the last three years
      `my weekly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for a weekly rate: your weekly rate of pay in dollars on the relevant day, without overtime, shift premiums and penalty rates
      `my earnings in the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for commission or payment by result: your total earnings in dollars over the weeks counted (12 months before the relevant day, leaving out whole weeks of unpaid leave and weeks of work injury absence with weekly payments)
      `my hours in the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for hourly, varied, casual or part-time work: the total hours you worked over the weeks counted (3 years before the relevant day, leaving out the same weeks)
      `the weeks counted` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of weeks counted (about 52 for 12 months, about 156 for 3 years)
      `my hourly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Only for hourly, varied, casual or part-time work: your hourly rate in dollars on the relevant day, without overtime, shift premiums and penalty rates
      `my employer gives me accommodation at work but not on leave` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer provides you with accommodation while you work but not while you are on leave
      `the weekly value of the accommodation` IS A NUMBER @desc The weekly value of that accommodation in dollars (under your award or agreement, or else its fair and reasonable value), 0 if none
      `what the rate is for` IS A `Purpose of the rate` @desc What the rate is for: long service leave; a payment instead of leave by agreement (cashing out); or a payment instead of leave when your service ends
GIVETH A `Rate answer`
`What is my ordinary weekly rate of pay` MEANS
    `the s 3(2) rate for` `how I am paid` `weekly` `my weekly rate of pay` `earnings` `my earnings in the weeks counted` `hours` `my hours in the weeks counted` `weeks` `the weeks counted` `hourly` `my hourly rate` `accommodation` `my employer gives me accommodation at work but not on leave` `value` `the weekly value of the accommodation` `for` `what the rate is for`

@export How much should I be paid for my long service leave, or for a payment instead of it (ss 8(1), 8(3a)(a), 8(4)(a))?
GIVEN `the weeks of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of leave being taken or paid out
      `my ordinary weekly rate of pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary weekly rate of pay in dollars (see the rate question)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much should I be paid for my leave` MEANS
    `the s 8 amount for` `the weeks of leave` `at` `my ordinary weekly rate of pay`

@export Is the way my employer is paying my long service leave one the Act allows (s 8(2))?
GIVEN `the way I am paid` IS A `Way of paying leave` @desc How the leave is being paid: in advance for the whole period of leave; on your usual paydays; another way you and your employer agreed; or another way you did not agree to
      `I asked in writing for a cheque by post` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only if paid on your usual paydays: whether you asked in writing for payment by cheque posted to an address you gave
GIVETH A `Way of paying answer`
`Is the way I am paid for my leave allowed` MEANS
    `the s 8(2) answer for` `the way I am paid` `cheque` `I asked in writing for a cheque by post`

@export My rate of pay changed while I was on long service leave, or after I cashed out leave: what more am I owed (s 8(3), (3a)(b))?
GIVEN `how the leave was paid` IS A `Kind of leave payment` @desc How the leave was paid: leave paid in advance; leave paid on the usual paydays; or a payment instead of leave by agreement (cashing out)
      `my old weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary weekly rate of pay before the change, in dollars
      `my new weekly rate` IS A NUMBER @desc Your ordinary weekly rate of pay after the change, in dollars
      `the weeks after the change` IS A NUMBER @desc The weeks of the leave (or of the leave cashed out) that fall after the change
      `the change came within the period of the leave cashed out` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only for cashing out: whether the change came within a period from the payment as long as the leave cashed out (for example within 13 weeks of cashing out 13 weeks)
GIVETH A `Variation answer`
`What more am I owed after a change in my rate` MEANS
    `the s 8(3) answer for` `how the leave was paid` `from` `my old weekly rate` `to` `my new weekly rate` `weeks` `the weeks after the change` `within` `the change came within the period of the leave cashed out`

§§ `Taking my leave`

@export Did my employer give me enough notice of the day my long service leave starts (s 7(3), (4)(c))?
GIVEN `the day I was told` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer gave you notice of the date your leave is to start
      `the first day of my leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your long service leave
      `we agreed to shorter notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you and your employer agreed to the leave on less than 60 days notice
GIVETH A `Notice answer`
`Did I get enough notice of my leave` MEANS
    `the s 7(3) answer for notice on` `the day I was told` `leave from` `the first day of my leave` `agreed` `we agreed to shorter notice`

@export What is the last day of my long service leave (s 7(7))?
GIVEN `the first day of my leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your long service leave
      `the days of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days of leave to be taken (as on your employer's statement; every day counts, including public holidays and days you would not normally work)
GIVETH A DATE
`What is the last day of my leave` MEANS
    `the s 7(7) last day of leave from` `the first day of my leave` `for` `the days of leave`

@export Did my employer give me the statement of my leave in time, before the leave started (s 10(6), Regulations reg 4(3), Form 2)?
GIVEN `the day my leave was granted` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer granted the leave
      `the first day of my leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your long service leave
      `I have been given the statement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have received the statement of the days of leave to be taken and the days remaining after it (Form 2)
      `the day I was given it` IS A DATE @desc The day you received it (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Statement answer`
`Did I get my leave statement in time` MEANS
    `the s 10(6) answer for leave granted on` `the day my leave was granted` `starting` `the first day of my leave` `given` `I have been given the statement` `on` `the day I was given it` `as of` `today`

@export May I work another job while I am on long service leave (s 14(1))?
GIVEN `the first day of my leave` IS A DATE @desc The first day of your long service leave
      `the days of leave` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days of leave (every day counts)
      `the job takes the place of my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the other job is employment in place of the employment in which you earned the leave (rather than, for example, a second job you already held alongside it)
      `the first day of the other job` IS A DATE @desc The first day you work, or would work, in the other job
GIVETH AN `Other work answer`
`May I work another job while on leave` MEANS
    `the s 14(1) answer for leave from` `the first day of my leave` `for` `the days of leave` `in place` `the job takes the place of my employment` `work from` `the first day of the other job`

§§ `When my service ends -- arises only when the employment has ended or the worker has died`

@export My service has ended: what long service leave payment am I owed, in weeks of pay (s 5(2)-(7))?
GIVEN `my completed years of service` IS A NUMBER @desc Your completed years of service when it ended
      `how it ended` IS A `How service ended` @desc How your service ended: you resigned lawfully; you ended your contract unlawfully (for example walking out without the notice your contract requires); your employer ended it, not for misconduct; your employer ended it on the ground of your serious and wilful misconduct; you retired; or the worker died (asked by the personal representative)
      `the weeks I have taken or been paid out` IS A NUMBER @desc Weeks of long service leave already taken (including in advance of the entitlement) or paid in lieu, 0 if none
GIVETH A `Termination answer`
`What am I owed when my service ends` MEANS
    `the s 5 termination answer for` `my completed years of service` `ended by` `how it ended` `used` `the weeks I have taken or been paid out`

@export Was my long service leave payment on termination paid on time (s 8(4)(b))?
GIVEN `the day my service ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your service was terminated (or the day of the worker's death)
      `the worker died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the service ended with the worker's death (you are the personal representative)
      `I have asked for it as personal representative` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Only after a death: whether you, as personal representative, have asked for the payment
      `the day I asked` IS A DATE @desc Only after a death: the day you asked (any date, if not yet)
      `it has been paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the payment has been made
      `the day it was paid` IS A DATE @desc The day it was paid (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Payment timing answer`
`Was my payment on termination on time` MEANS
    `the s 8(4)(b) answer for` `the day my service ended` `died` `the worker died` `asked` `I have asked for it as personal representative` `on` `the day I asked` `paid` `it has been paid` `on` `the day it was paid` `as of` `today`

@export I took long service leave before I was entitled to it and then my service ended: how much can my employer deduct from my final pay (s 7(6))?
GIVEN `I took the leave in advance of the entitlement` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you took the leave by agreement before the entitlement to it had accrued (s 7(4)(d))
      `my service ended before the entitlement accrued` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service ended, for any reason, before the entitlement to that leave accrued
      `the amount I was paid for the leave` IS A NUMBER @desc What you were paid for the leave taken in advance, in dollars
      `the payment instead of leave I would have had` IS A NUMBER @desc The payment instead of leave you would have been entitled to when your service ended had you not taken leave in advance, in dollars (0 if none, for example under 7 years)
GIVETH A `Deduction answer`
`How much can my employer deduct for leave taken in advance` MEANS
    `the s 7(6) answer for` `I took the leave in advance of the entitlement` `ended before accrual` `my service ended before the entitlement accrued` `paid` `the amount I was paid for the leave` `would have had` `the payment instead of leave I would have had`

§§ `Records, enforcement and offences`

@export Can I see my employer's long service leave records about me, and for how long must they be kept (s 10(2)(c), (5))?
GIVEN `my service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your service with the employer has ended
      `the day it ended` IS A DATE @desc The day your service ended (any date, if it has not)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Records answer`
`Can I see my long service leave records` MEANS
    `the s 10 records answer for` `my service has ended` `ended on` `the day it ended` `as of` `today`

@export Can I apply to the South Australian Employment Tribunal for an order that my employer grant my leave or pay me, and am I in time (s 13(1), (2), (4))?
GIVEN `who is applying` IS AN `Applicant` @desc Who is applying: the worker; the personal representative of a worker who died; a registered association the worker belongs to, with the worker's consent; such an association without the worker's consent; the complainant in a prosecution in which the employer was found guilty of not complying with an inspector's notice; or someone else
      `the worker died` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has died
      `leave was not granted or a payment was not received` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was not granted long service leave in accordance with the Act, or did not receive a payment due under it
      `the service has ended` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's service has ended
      `the day the service ended` IS A DATE @desc The day the service ended (any date, if it has not)
      `I have applied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the application has been made
      `the day I applied` IS A DATE @desc The day of the application (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH AN `Order answer`
`Can I apply to SAET for my leave or payment` MEANS
    `the s 13 answer for` `who is applying` `died` `the worker died` `not granted or not paid` `leave was not granted or a payment was not received` `ended` `the service has ended` `on` `the day the service ended` `applied` `I have applied` `on` `the day I applied` `as of` `today`

@export My employer kept no proper long service leave records: will SAET accept what I say about my service or my hours (s 13(3))?
GIVEN `my employer kept proper records` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer kept proper long service leave records as the Act requires
      `what is disputed` IS A `What is in issue` @desc What is disputed: the period of your service; the average hours you worked each week over a period; or something else
      `SAET has ruled for me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether SAET, considering it fair to you, has ruled that what you say will be accepted as proved unless the employer proves otherwise
GIVETH A `Records presumption answer`
`Will SAET accept my account without records` MEANS
    `the s 13(3) answer for` `my employer kept proper records` `issue` `what is disputed` `ruled` `SAET has ruled for me`

@export An inspector has directed my employer to grant my leave or pay me: by when must my employer comply (s 12)?
GIVEN `the day my employer received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day your employer received the inspector's written notice
      `the days stated in the notice` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of days the notice gives your employer to comply
      `my employer applied for review` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer applied to SAET for a review of the notice
      `the day of the review application` IS A DATE @desc The day it applied for review (any date, if it did not)
      `my employer has complied` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your employer has granted the leave or made the payment
      `the day it complied` IS A DATE @desc The day it did so (any date, if not yet)
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A `Direction answer`
`By when must my employer comply with the inspector` MEANS
    `the s 12 answer for a notice received on` `the day my employer received the notice` `days` `the days stated in the notice` `review` `my employer applied for review` `on` `the day of the review application` `complied` `my employer has complied` `on` `the day it complied` `as of` `today`

@export What is the most my employer (or I) can be fined for a long service leave offence, and by when must a prosecution start (ss 10, 11(3), 12(6), 14, 15)?
GIVEN `the offence` IS AN `Offence` @desc The offence: not keeping the long service leave records; not recording a cashing-out agreement in writing, giving you a copy, or keeping it; not passing the records on to a related employer; not giving you the statement before your leave; not giving you the statement when leave was cashed out; obstructing an inspector or not complying with an inspector's requirement; not complying with an inspector's notice to grant leave or pay; engaging a worker known to be on long service leave so that the worker breaches s 14(1); or your own other employment in place of your employment while on leave
      `the day of the offence` IS A DATE @desc The day the offence is said to have been committed
GIVETH AN `Offence answer`
`What is the fine and the time to prosecute` MEANS
    `the offence answer for` `the offence` `committed on` `the day of the offence`
